# Retired project-local harnesses/generator outputs: do not accidentally commit
# them if an external tool recreates them. Pi is the only maintained harness.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.securecoder/
swark-output/

# Whitelist docs build dependency manifest (the global *.txt rule above
# catches recovery dumps; pinned-dep manifests must ship).
!docs/requirements-docs.txt

# Pi project resources, sessions, and shared local guidance stay on this laptop.
# These are useful development context, but are not shipped application files.
.pi/
.agent/
AGENTS.md

# Private local issue tracker and planning workspace.
.scratch/

# Vendored wordlists carry their own provenance: generate.py is committed so the
# corpus can be regenerated and audited, and manifest.json pins the digest of the
# exact bytes shipped. These are attack input, so their contents must be reviewable
# in the diff like any other input rather than fetched at build time.
!src/app/pentesting/catalogs/wordlists/*.txt

# UI-triggered update handshake (request/status files written at runtime)
.control/
.deploy-backups/
